\viewkind4\uc1\pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par Forty days and forty nights\cf0 
\par  Thou wast fasting in the wild,
\par  Forty days and forty nights
\par  Tempted, and yet undefiled, -
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   2.  Sunbeams scorching all the day,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0   Chilly dewdrops nightly shed,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1  \cf0 Prowling beasts about Thy way,
\par  Stones Thy pillow, earth Thy bed.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   3. Shall we not Thy sorrow share,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  And from earthly joys abstain,
\par   Fasting with unceasing prayer,
\par   Glad with Thee to suffer pain?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   4.  And if Satan, vexing sore,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  Flesh or spirit should assail,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Thou, his Vanquisher before,
\par Grant we may not faint nor fail.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. So shall we have peace divine;
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Holier gladness ours shall be;
\par Round us too shall angels shine,
\par \pard       Such as ministered to Thee.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

